SIMD emboldening model and deferred hardware checks
=================================================

Host-side model test:

    sh tests/run_retro_simd_models.sh

Or compile the deterministic model manually:

    cc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -fsanitize=address,undefined \
       tests/mmi_embolden_equivalence.c -o mmi-embolden-test
    ./mmi-embolden-test

It models byte-level QFSRV neighbour extraction, saturated PADDUB, MMI
POR (16 bytes), and VIS1 FOR (8 bytes).  It now covers 72,000
combinations including both pitch directions, all 16 byte alignments,
short and long rows, 0..4 horizontal strength, and multiple grayscale
limits.  It also checks the untouched guard and padding bytes.

IMPORTANT: The host model cannot execute R5900 or VIS1 machine code.
The MMI/VIS1 kernels still require separate target compiler checks,
pixel-identity tests against unoptimized FreeType, and hardware
benchmarks.  Deferred target testing is described in
docs/MMI_EMBOLDEN.md and docs/VIS1_EMBOLDEN.md.

Packed conversion batch tests
=============================

The same host batch command also runs tests/convert_simd_model.c with
197,376 MMI/VIS1 packed conversion cases.  No hardware-specific code
is run by this model.

To compare the actual FreeType conversion output after building scalar
and SIMD library variants separately, build
`tests/convert_freetype_compare.c` against each variant.  It computes a
fingerprint for 16,560 deterministic cases; compare the entire lines.
Only active pixels are hashed, not potentially uninitialized row padding.

See docs/RETRO_BITMAP_CONVERT.md and docs/RETRO_SIMD_TEST_PLAN.md.

BGRA blending (common portable integer fast paths)
=================================================

The same host batch command also compiles and runs
`tests/blend_exact255_model.c`, which enumerates all 65,026 possible
numerators of an 8-bit by 8-bit product and compares 35,840 complete
BGRA rows against the original FreeType arithmetic. Both direct and
adaptive lookup-table routines are exercised in the byte model.

Compile `tests/blend_freetype_compare.c` with scalar and optimized
FreeType builds separately to fingerprint 11,520 public-API blend cases.
Because the upstream BGRA negative-pitch path is not yet implemented,
only positive-pitch blend API inputs are used in this test.

See `docs/RETRO_BITMAP_BLEND.md`.

LCD 5-tap filtering (FT_CONFIG_OPTION_SUBPIXEL_RENDERING only)
==============================================================

The host batch runner also includes tests/lcd_spans_model.c.
It exercises 165,120 deterministic horizontal and vertical
five-tap span cases with odd lengths, varying byte alignments,
multiple weights/coverages, overlapping spans and both pitch signs.
The test uses the actual portable folded implementation.

FT_CONFIG_OPTION_RETRO_LCD_SPANS provides portable folding.
FT_CONFIG_OPTION_MMI_LCD_SPANS additionally uses the R5900 PADDB
wrapping byte-add SIMD for long spans. The MMI assembly has not
been run by this host model and needs later target verification.

For LCD glyph output comparisons, enable
FT_CONFIG_OPTION_SUBPIXEL_RENDERING in both scalar and accelerated
FreeType builds, then compare retro_glyph_hash lcd/lcd-v outputs.
See docs/RETRO_LCD_SPANS.md.
